## 10. Development loop

| Task | Command |
|---|---|
| Foreground dev session (live sync TUI) | `cinna dev` |
| Run a script in the remote env | `cinna exec python scripts/main.py` |
| Run any command in the remote env | `cinna exec <command>` |
| Install a Python package | `cinna exec uv pip install <pkg>` then add to `workspace_requirements.txt` |
| Sync status from another terminal | `cinna sync status` |
| List conflict copies | `cinna sync conflicts` |
| Talk to the agent to test it (conversation) | `cinna chat "<message>"` |
| Refresh expired CLI token | `cinna set-token <token_or_url>` |

Iteration: edit files locally → Mutagen syncs them remotely within seconds → `cinna exec <cmd>` runs the script; stdout/stderr stream back live; exit code matches → inspect `app-data/storage/` for output.

> **Test it end-to-end by talking to it.** `cinna exec` proves a script runs; a **conversation** proves the *agent* works — same permission checks, agent-env calls, and model/SDK as production. From inside this workspace run `cinna chat "<message>"` (the agent is inferred; no `--agent` needed). **Before writing test messages, read [`./CHAT_TESTING.md`](./CHAT_TESTING.md)** — it explains how to phrase them like a real, in-a-hurry user (terse, missing details) instead of a precise agent prompt, which is what actually catches production bugs. Output is **NDJSON** — one JSON event per line; read the `content` of `message` events with `"role":"agent"` for the reply, capture the `session_id` from the first `session` event, and continue with `cinna chat --resume <session_id> "<follow-up>"`. Each `message` also carries an `events` array — the agent's thinking blocks and tool calls (with their input payloads) and tool results — so you can debug *why* it answered as it did (`--no-events` to omit). Attach a fixture with `--file path/to/input.csv`; files the agent attaches back land in `./cinna-chat-files/<session_id>/`. Sync edited prompts/scripts first (`cinna dev`, or `cinna sync push`) so you're chatting against the new behavior. **Requires** this agent to be synced under an account workspace (i.e. via `cinna agent sync`) — `cinna chat` uses the account session API; in a standalone `cinna setup` workspace it has no account context.

Conflicts: Mutagen writes `<file>.conflict.<side>.<timestamp>` instead of picking a winner. Open in the editor, pick a winner, delete the conflict copy.

